{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkJNM9sCDiNhRdgyNSr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user has a payments PR that needs review from their co-founder who's on a flight until tomorrow morning. They want to make the review faster - specifically take 10 minutes instead of an hour. They're asking what they could put in front of the co-founder to help.\n\nThis is about preparing materials for code review. They want to maximize the efficiency of the review process. I should think about what would help a reviewer move through a PR quickly:\n\n1. A summary of what changed and why\n2. The migration strategy explained clearly\n3. Key decisions and trade-offs highlighted\n4. Testing evidence\n5. A visual diff or walkthrough\n6. Risk assessment\n7. Links to related context\n\nThe most valuable thing for a quick review is probably:\n- A clear PR description that explains the migration strategy and key decisions\n- A summary of files changed and what each one does\n- Key decision points highlighted\n- Any risks or gotchas called out\n\nI could suggest:\n1. Adding a detailed PR description if one doesn't exist\n2. Creating a quick visual guide or diagram of the migration\n3. Adding comments in the code to highlight key changes\n4. Creating a migration test plan or validation checklist\n5. Adding a before/after comparison\n\nBut I should probably ask to see the PR first, or at least understand what the migration is about. Actually, the user is asking for general advice on what could help. Let me think about what's most effective:\n\nThe most high-impact things for accelerating code review of a migration:\n1. **Clear PR description** - explains the migration strategy, why it was done this way, any gotchas\n2. **Annotated diff or visual breakdown** - showing key sections with context\n3. **Migration validation checklist** - showing what was tested\n4. **Risk summary** - what could go wrong and how we're mitigating it\n\nI should give them 2-3 concrete suggestions ranked by impact. A tight PR description is the foundation. But I could also offer to add inline comments, create a review guide, or other high-impact materials.\nA well-structured PR description is the quickest win here—it should walk through the migration strategy, explain key decisions, and flag any potential gotchas. Beyond that, inline code comments highlighting critical sections and a testing checklist showing what's been validated would help the reviewer move through this much faster than reading the full diff cold.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6946,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6946},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"cb914237-e095-4e6f-847b-8bdf5ec4dae0","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:51:05.040Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkJMQbzVcwywxUvKkwd"}
